# Independently authored SHOW empty-result stubs sentinel
# smoke for the GPL MTR-format runner. NOT copied or adapted
# from MySQL's mysql-test/.
#
# Existing coverage (do NOT duplicate):
#   - variable_basic_extra.test:107-133 already pins SHOW
#     VARIABLES / VARIABLES LIKE / STATUS / WARNINGS /
#     ENGINES / PROCESSLIST. Same `--echo === KNOWN
#     DIVERGENCE ===` + empty-result framing.
#   - charset_collation_basic_extra.test:78-80 pins SHOW
#     COLLATION (and :116-118 for SHOW COLLATION LIKE).
#   - variable_basic_extra.test:85-87 also pins SHOW
#     COLLATION via a second framing.
#   - auth_basic_extra.test:74-80 pins SHOW GRANTS and
#     SHOW GRANTS FOR 'u'@'h'.
#   - show_basic_extra.test pins SHOW DATABASES / TABLES /
#     COLUMNS / CREATE TABLE / TABLES LIKE.
#
# After full duplicate audit, only THREE empty-stub SHOWs
# remain uncovered:
#   - SHOW ERRORS
#   - SHOW CHARSET (the CHARSET-only variant, not COLLATION)
#   - SHOW PRIVILEGES
# This slice pins exactly those three. Initial draft of this
# slice over-claimed coverage gaps; narrowed after review
# pointed out the duplicates.
#
# Big-picture finding:
#   zeta's MySQL shim has TWO classes of empty-result SHOW
#   dispatch:
#     - SHOW WARNINGS routes to MySqlResult::Warnings
#       (3-column shape).
#     - SHOW VARIABLES/STATUS/ERRORS/CHARSET/PRIVILEGES route
#       to MySqlResult::EmptyShow (2-column shape:
#       Variable_name, Value). SHOW ERRORS technically has
#       the wrong shape (MySQL gives Level/Code/Message),
#       but the empty rendering masks this.
#   The MTR format only emits the header line when there's
#   at least one row — so this shape-divergence is invisible
#   in the recorded .result. Pinning these documents the
#   no-error parse path; a future fix that wires real data
#   would also need to fix the column shape.
#
# Adaptation notes:
#   # zeta-adapt: SHOW ERRORS, SHOW CHARSET, SHOW PRIVILEGES
#     all execute without error but return EMPTY result sets.
#   # zeta-adapt: If you need actual server-state introspection,
#     query information_schema / pg_catalog directly — those
#     surfaces are at least partially populated.

--echo === SHOW ERRORS — empty stub (MySQL: Level/Code/Message; zeta empty) ===

SHOW ERRORS;

--echo === SHOW CHARSET — empty stub ===

# Distinct from charset_collation_basic_extra.test (which
# covers SHOW COLLATION, NOT SHOW CHARSET).
SHOW CHARSET;

--echo === SHOW PRIVILEGES — empty stub ===

SHOW PRIVILEGES;
